cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "rtclock: real-time timing arithmetic and schedulability analysis for Python control loops"
version: 0.1.0
date-released: 2026-10-04
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  Monotonic timebase abstraction with a measured (not assumed) resolution,
  period and deadline arithmetic with units, a fixed-rate loop driver that
  reports drift rather than absorbing it, latency histograms with explicitly
  named percentile semantics, rate-monotonic and EDF utilization bounds,
  response-time analysis, priority-ceiling blocking, and timing-budget
  composition. Validation level 1, educational to research grade. Not
  flight-qualified, not certified, not approved for operational aerospace use.
authors:
  - name: "OPTIMA Organisation"
keywords:
  - real-time
  - scheduling
  - rate-monotonic
  - response-time-analysis
  - latency
  - percentile
  - control-loop
